From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sram: allwinner,sun4i-a10-system-control: Add
 the A733

The A733 has a system control block at 0x03000000 like the earlier
SoCs, but none of the registers the A64 compatible stands for: its
EMAC clock register lives in the GMAC itself. What it holds and Linux
needs is the resistor calibration of the USB PHYs.

Add a compatible of its own, without the A64 fallback.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the system control node
with this compatible binds the driver without the A64 fallback.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/sram/allwinner,sun4i-a10-system-control.yaml        | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/allwinner,sun4i-a10-system-control.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/allwinner,sun4i-a10-system-control.yaml
index 6e6ab2168a2a..4d3445a87f14 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/allwinner,sun4i-a10-system-control.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/allwinner,sun4i-a10-system-control.yaml
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ properties:
           - allwinner,sun50i-a64-system-control
           - allwinner,sun50i-h5-system-control
           - allwinner,sun50i-h616-system-control
+          - allwinner,sun60i-a733-system-control
       - items:
           - enum:
               - allwinner,suniv-f1c100s-system-control
